! ambiguous-precedence: operator `<<` has lower precedence than `+`
  @ test.idl:2:22

 2 │ const long test1 = 1 << 2 + 3;
   │                      ˆˆ ˆˆˆˆˆ than this expression
   │                      └─ this operator has lower precedence
 3 │ const long test2 = 1 + 2 << 3;
 4 │ const long test3 = 1 >> 2 - 3;

  ? add parentheses to clarify the intended order of operations

! ambiguous-precedence: operator `>>` has lower precedence than `-`
  @ test.idl:4:22

 2 │ const long test1 = 1 << 2 + 3;
 3 │ const long test2 = 1 + 2 << 3;
 4 │ const long test3 = 1 >> 2 - 3;
   │                      ˆˆ ˆˆˆˆˆ than this expression
   │                      └─ this operator has lower precedence
 5 │ const long test4 = 1 - 2 >> 3;

  ? add parentheses to clarify the intended order of operations
